  { number := 107, text := "### 3.2 Systems Lean component" },
  { number := 108, text := "" },
  { number := 109, text := "The language and compiler path specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md). For the Systems Lean component of Lean Machine, that path is REQUIRED. Systems Lean produces freestanding high assurance C compiled ahead of time, on assurance levels a Rust type system is not expressive enough to prove, compiled with CompCert `ccomp`. CompCert verified compilation and a bootstrapped Slake compiler that fully typechecks remain REQUIRED for that named high assurance path. Future versions MAY target LLVM IR so the Rust ecosystem can be upgraded without a pile of `-sys` crates. Those four language pins live in the Systems Lean product tree. They are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`." },
