  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "## 5. Required Conformance" },
  { number := 221, text := "" },
  { number := 222, text := "Work that claims this specification conforms if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 223, text := "" },
  { number := 224, text := "1. Numbered markdown is the contract humans read; the specification is also encoded in Lean; proofs live in separate Lean modules; Formal Vibefication citations keep the canonical Proof of Keags URLs; `spec_check` remains form and is not meaning (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 225, text := "2. Important Lean Machine work is Unlicense as specified in `0009_PDOSS.md`; a copyright grant that keeps a later private claim is not treated as enough freedom for that work; this document does not invent a second PDOSS specification (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 226, text := "3. The Systems Lean component follows `0002_Systems_Lean.md`; named high assurance work on that component emits freestanding C compiled ahead of time, compiles that emit with CompCert `ccomp`, and keeps a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks; those steps are not optional because a pin is missing from this repository's `ref/` (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 227, text := "4. Legal Lean, when present, exposes contradictions and proves legal concerns; Legal Lean has no separate stack number; Legal Lean is not treated as finished (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 228, text := "5. Holy Lean, when present, encodes scripture as a practical set of rules; Holy Lean has no separate stack number; Holy Lean is not treated as implemented (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 229, text := "6. The machine attempts to answer questions deterministically; a timestamped note is written when an answer is wrong or imprecise (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 230, text := "7. The design is a distributed system that consumes information and builds a better version of itself, citing `0006_RSI.md`; that design is not treated as a claim that the machine already runs (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 231, text := "8. Worship and belief are not treated as a conformance conjunct for the compiler or for Lean Machine software (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 232, text := "9. A conforming Lean Machine is not claimed to exist; Legal Lean and Holy Lean are treated as ongoing named work; beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration are treated as ongoing and not ready for use; fargo, SSSP, and Carbonado remain unspecified; a numbered Vocabulary file does not exist (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 233, text := "10. Every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean`; proofs of those encodings live in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`; the named gate in `0007_CI.md` remains the gate (Clause 4.10)." },
  { number := 234, text := "" },
  { number := 235, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming Lean Machine. Meeting these items is a claim about work that claims this specification, not about this markdown file as a shipped engine." },
  { number := 236, text := "" },
  { number := 237, text := "Optional recommendations (SHOULD, RECOMMENDED) and the MAY LLVM IR path do not break conformance when unmet, but authors SHOULD follow them unless there is a clear reason not to. Clause 4.8 is informative. Belief is not a conformance conjunct." },
  { number := 238, text := "" },
  { number := 239, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 240, text := "" },
  { number := 241, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 242, text := "" },
  { number := 243, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 244, text := "" },
  { number := 245, text := "1. fargo is not specified. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, 0011, 0012, 0013, or 0014 for fargo." },
  { number := 246, text := "2. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is not specified. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 247, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Unlicense remains the license. Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is Surmount Systems Tech Tree (`0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.md`). Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`). Number 0013 is this specification. Number 0014 is Anunnaki Encoding (`0014_Anunnaki_Encoding.md`). This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 248, text := "4. Legal Lean is a named component of Lean Machine. Legal Lean has no separate numbered specification and no assigned number of its own. This document MUST NOT be read as creating `NNNN_Legal_Lean.md`. Treating Legal Lean as having a separate stack number is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 249, text := "5. Holy Lean is a named component of Lean Machine. Holy Lean has no separate numbered specification and no assigned number of its own. This document MUST NOT be read as creating `NNNN_Holy_Lean.md`. Treating Holy Lean as having a separate stack number is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 250, text := "6. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present." },
  { number := 251, text := "" },
  { number := 252, text := "### 6.2 Product that is not implemented" },
  { number := 253, text := "" },
  { number := 254, text := "1. Lean Machine work is ongoing and is not ready for use. A conforming implementation is not claimed. This specification records the contract. It does not ship the machine. Treating a conforming Lean Machine as existing is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 255, text := "2. Legal Lean is ongoing named work. Automatic proof of legal concerns is not claimed done. Treating Legal Lean as finished is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 256, text := "3. Holy Lean is ongoing named work. A Lean encoding of scripture as a civilization set of rules is not claimed done. Treating Holy Lean as implemented is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 257, text := "4. Distributed self improvement is a design requirement. A running distributed machine is not claimed. Treating that design requirement as a claim that such a machine already runs is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 258, text := "5. Timestamped notes on wrong or imprecise answers are a requirement. A shipped store for those notes is not claimed." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "### 6.3 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "1. beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, and Continuous Integration remain ongoing and not ready for use. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 263, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md`. This document does not claim that match already holds." },
  { number := 264, text := "3. Neurosymbolic integration remains in `0004_SSSSS.md`. It is specified there. It is not a shipped product. This document does not move it here." },
  { number := 265, text := "4. `lean/LeanMachineSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean` proves those claims. `0013_Lean_Machine.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0013.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that a Lean Machine product exists. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use. A mash of spec encodings and proofs in one module is Cons False in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`." },
  { number := 266, text := "" },
  { number := 267, text := "### 6.4 Pins and licenses this document does not add" },
  { number := 268, text := "" },
  { number := 269, text := "1. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are not pins of this specifications repository's `ref/`. `0002_Systems_Lean.md` places those Form 1 pins in the Systems Lean product tree. This repository MUST NOT copy those four trees into this repository's `ref/`." },
  { number := 270, text := "2. https://unlicense.org is informative prior art. It is not a Clause 12 pin. The binding dedication is `UNLICENSE.md` as specified in `0009_PDOSS.md`." },
  { number := 271, text := "3. Formal Vibefication essays are cited by URL. They are not Clause 12 pins. This repository does not vendor those essays as Form 2 copies under `ref/`. Full license text is still not published on https://proofofkeags.com . Do not invent that license." },
  { number := 272, text := "" },
  { number := 273, text := "### 6.5 Informative items this document names" },
