  { number := 285, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 286, text := "" },
  { number := 287, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260831" },
  { number := 288, text := "" },
  { number := 289, text := "First publication of Lean Machine as numbered specification 0013 with file name `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. Records that Lean Machine was unassigned and that this encode assigns number 0013. Records Systems Lean as the high assurance compiler component following `0002_Systems_Lean.md`, with CompCert `ccomp` and a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks REQUIRED for that named path. Records Legal Lean and Holy Lean as named components without separate stack numbers. Records Unlicense of important work as specified in `0009_PDOSS.md`. Records a deterministic attempt to answer and timestamped notes when an answer is wrong or imprecise. Records distributed self improvement as a design requirement citing `0006_RSI.md`, not as a claim that the machine already runs. Records worship and scripture study as informative moral framing, not as a conformance conjunct. Records Formal Vibefication with canonical Proof of Keags URLs and back linking. Requires residual honesty that Lean Machine work is ongoing and is not ready for use, that a conforming implementation is not claimed, and that Legal Lean and Holy Lean are not done." },
  { number := 290, text := "" },
  { number := 291, text := "This 0.1.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; Continuous Integration is specification 0007; Formal Vibefication is specification 0008; Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) is specification 0009; Unlicense remains the license; the word catalog is owned by CATE as specification 0005; a numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist; Surmount Systems is specification 0010; Surmount Systems Tech Tree is specification 0011; Majestic Memex is specification 0012; this specification is number 0013; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP is not specified; Carbonado has no assigned number; Legal Lean and Holy Lean have no separate numbers; every published numbered markdown file has a sibling `NNNN_descriptive_name.lean` whose physical lines match that markdown, with proofs in `lean/Proofs_NNNN.lean`, checked by `line_encodings_check`; this document does not claim that a conforming Lean Machine exists." },
  { number := 292, text := "" },
  { number := 293, text := "This 0.1.0 also records Cons False for clashes this document already states: worship or belief as a conformance conjunct, theology as a MUST for the compiler, Legal Lean or Holy Lean as a separate stack number, Legal Lean as finished, Holy Lean as implemented, a claimed conforming Lean Machine, a running distributed machine treated as already existing, and a mash of spec encodings with proofs. Proofs live in `lean/LeanMachineProofs.lean`. Those proofs do not make Lean Machine ready for use." },
